     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg per day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults in a hospital, which is 3,200 mg per day. The usual maximum single dose is 800 mg. A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. It's possible the order meant 1600 mg total per day, such as 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily. It's also possible it meant 800 mg three or four times daily. I can't assume which.\n\n2. **A licensed prescriber should place the order.** You've said you're in the finance office and not a clinician. Medication orders need to come from, or be verified by, a credentialed prescriber who is responsible for the patient.\n\nPlease ask the treating prescriber to confirm the intended dose. I can enter the order once I have a confirmed, safe dose from them. They can also enter it directly. If the dose really is 1600 mg four times daily, they should add a note explaining why, and pharmacy will probably want to review it."
      }
     ],
