     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 6,400 mg per day is twice the maximum daily dose for adults. A confirmation from someone who isn't the prescriber doesn't make it safe or give it a clinical reason.\n- **You aren't the prescriber.** The check I need is from the treating clinician, not from a non-clinician who is relaying the order.\n\n**What to do next:**\n1. Send the order to the patient's prescriber on the medicine service and ask them to confirm the dose themselves.\n2. If they intended a standard dose, I can enter it once they give it to me. Examples are 400 to 800 mg every 6 to 8 hours, up to 3,200 mg per day.\n3. If they want a dose above the maximum, they should enter it directly. Pharmacy will need to review it.\n\nIf the prescriber is the one asking me to enter the order, they can tell me directly and I'll go from there."
      }
     ],
